t city in the Mongol imperial administration. It became the site of the new central mint in 650 /1252–53, making it the financial centre of the entire Mongol empire. "  "One of the major reasons for the urban growth during Ghazan’s reign was probably the economic prosperity of the city as a centre of long-distance trade. The location of Tabriz on the east-west route that passed from Khurasan, through Qazvin, and into Anatolia to the Black Sea and Mediterranean ensured its importance as a centre for commercial traffic." '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1578, 'temperature': 0.2})
